# Workflow Example: Prompt to Code

Purpose:
  Immutable example showing how a prompt flows through the SDDRA system.
  This example demonstrates the complete chain execution from P1 to DEP1.

Example Prompt:
  "Create a payment module with refund functionality"

Execution Flow:
  D0 (default)
    ↓
  P1 (prompt)
    Input: "Create a payment module with refund functionality"
    Output: docs/00-about/project.md, docs/20-architecture/overview.md
    Token: in=500, out=1200, delta=700
    Decision: DEC-100 proposed (Payment module architecture)
    Gate: human_required
    ↓
  D0 (default)
    ↓
  D1 (docs)
    Input: prompt + DEC-100
    Output: docs/30-backend/overview.md, docs/60-database/overview.md
    Token: in=1200, out=3500, delta=2300
    Decision: DEC-101 proposed (PostgreSQL for payments), DEC-102 proposed (Refund workflow)
    Gate: human_required
    ↓
  D0 (default)
    ↓
  S1 (sdd)
    Input: docs/ + approved decisions
    Output: .sdd/project/domains.sdd, .sdd/instances/vkard.az/tasks/TASK-201.sdd
    Token: in=3500, out=5800, delta=2300
    Decision: DEC-100, DEC-101, DEC-102 approved
    Gate: human_required
    ↓
  D0 (default)
    ↓
  C1 (code)
    Input: .sdd/project/ + approved decisions
    Output: project/backend/payment/service.go, project/backend/payment/refund.go
    Token: in=5800, out=42000, delta=36200
    Decision: DEC-100, DEC-101, DEC-102 status → implemented
    Gate: none
    ↓
  D0 (default)
    ↓
  R1 (review)
    Input: project/
    Output: approval
    Token: in=42000, out=500, delta=41500
    Gate: human_required
    ↓
  D0 (default)
    ↓
  DEP1 (deploy)
    Input: project/ + approval
    Output: production
    Token: in=500, out=1200, delta=700
    Gate: human_required
    ↓
  D0 (default)

Artifacts Created:
  docs/
    00-about/project.md
    20-architecture/overview.md
    30-backend/overview.md
    60-database/overview.md
  70-api/overview.md

  .sdd/project/
    domains.sdd
    tasks/TASK-201.sdd
    decisions/DEC-100.sdd, DEC-101.sdd, DEC-102.sdd

  project/
    backend/payment/service.go
    backend/payment/refund.go
    backend/payment/repository.go
    backend/payment/refund_test.go

State: +
  Note:
  This is an EXAMPLE workflow. Actual execution follows the same pattern
  but with real prompts, real decisions, and real code. The chain graph
  is unbreakable — every arm returns to D0.
